<p>
  <alert>Section 14.7 - Structure of abelian groups</alert>
</p>

<p>
  <ul>
  
    <li>
      <p>
        Results to know:
      </p>

      <p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>
              Theorem 14.7.3, Corollary 14.7.6, Theorem 14.7.7
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              <m>\mathbb{Z}_{ab}\cong \mathbb{Z}_{a}\times \mathbb{Z}_{b}</m> when <m>\gcd(a,b)=1</m>.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>

    <li>
      <p>
        Be able to:
      </p>

      <p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>
              Given an abelian group described by generators and relations, write it as a product of cyclic group of prime power order and <m>\mathbb{Z}^{a}</m>, by employing diagonalization.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Classify (up to isomorphism) all abelian groups of a given order.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Use the uniqueness in the structure theorem to prove results.
            </p>
          </li>

  
        </ul>
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</p>

<p>
