    <li>
      <p>
        Be able to:
      </p>

      <p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <p>
              Explain why a finite field <m>F</m> must have <m>p^k</m> elements, where <m>p</m> is the characteristic of <m>F</m> and <m>k=[K:\mathbb Z_p]</m>
  
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Explain why the characteristic of an integral domain is either <m>0</m> or a prime number. 
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Explain why a finite field can be generated by a single element, that is, <m>F=\mathbb Z_p(\alpha)</m> for some <m>\alpha</m>, where <m>\alpha</m> is a generator of the cyclic group <m>F^{\times}</m>. 
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <p>
              Solve a variety of problems about finite fields; see the hw. 
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </p>
